@startuml archive-handover-flow

' Reader-facing flow for the German archive handover guide: how a dispatched
' invoice mail reaches the operator's e-mail archive. Two rows keep the figure
' compact on a page: the application on top, the mail provider below. Orthogonal
' edges keep every arrow straight. Edge labels are kept off the horizontal edges
' (ortho places them onto the boxes); the status feedback and the journaling
' variant are notes instead of labelled back-edges, so no line crosses another.

' A single generic family: PlantUML quotes a comma list as one family name in SVG,
' which browsers cannot match and fall back to serif.
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
hide stereotype
skinparam roundCorner 0
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam ranksep 60

skinparam rectangle {
  FontSize 11
  FontStyle bold
  FontColor #ffffff
  BorderColor #2D66B0
}
skinparam rectangle<<group>> {
  FontColor #5F6368
  FontStyle bold
  BackgroundColor transparent
  BorderColor #DADCE0
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
  BorderColor #DADCE0
  FontColor #202124
}

rectangle "Little Trotter X-Invoice" <<group>> as App {
  rectangle "1 Finale E-Rechnung erstellen\n<color:#D5E8FF>PDF mit XML, Zeitpunkt protokolliert</color>" as Issue #1A73E8
  rectangle "2 E-Mail erstellen\n<color:#D5E8FF>Original gesichert, Prüfsumme und Signatur</color>" as Compose #1A73E8
  Issue -right-> Compose
}

rectangle "Ihr E-Mail-Anbieter / Ihre IT" <<group>> as Provider {
  rectangle "3 Postausgangsserver des Betriebs\n<color:#E8EAED>verschlüsselte Übergabe</color>" as Smtp #5F6368
  rectangle "4a Empfänger\n<color:#E8EAED>Übertragung 1: an Kunden</color>" as Customer #5F6368
  rectangle "4b Archivadresse (Option B)\n<color:#E8EAED>Übertragung 2: separate SMTP-Session</color>" as ArchiveAddr #5F6368
  rectangle "5 E-Mail-Archiv (Anbieter oder eigene IT)\n<color:#D7F0DC>unveränderbar, 8 Jahre</color>" as Archive #188038
  Smtp -right-> Customer : Übertragung 1
  Smtp -down-> ArchiveAddr : Übertragung 2 (nach Quittung 1)
  ArchiveAddr -right-> Archive
  Smtp .[#188038]down.> Archive
}

Compose -down-> Smtp : verschlüsselt

note right of Archive
  Gestrichelt, Option A (Standard):
  der Anbieter kopiert die Nachricht
  selbst ins Archiv
end note

note bottom of ArchiveAddr
  Option B: separate SMTP-Übertragung
  ohne Bcc-Kopfzeile. Ein Fehler im
  Archiv gefährdet den Kundenversand nie.
end note

@enduml
